@@ -2,7 +2,13 @@
 
 Native Node.js binding for nftables via libnftnl + libmnl. Manages IPv4/IPv6 firewall tables with dynamic IP sets, port blocking, named counters, and timeout support through direct netlink communication — no shell commands, no `nft` CLI.
 
-Requires Node.js ≥ 24 and a Linux kernel ≥ 5.7 with `CAP_NET_ADMIN` or root.
+Requires Node.js ≥ 24 and Linux with `CAP_NET_ADMIN` or root.
+
+A kernel ≥ 5.7 is recommended. On older kernels `createTable()` transparently
+retries without the features they lack — per-element counters first, then
+`NFT_SET_CONCAT`, then counters altogether — giving up as little as possible at
+each step. Blocking and timeouts work regardless, and a kernel that only lacks
+`NFT_SET_EXPR` keeps its named per-set counters.
 
